sections.statement:
From Bohr theory:

$$E_n=-\frac{me^4}{2n^2h^2}
=-109700\ \mathrm{cm^{-1}}\times\frac{1}{n^2}\times\left(\frac m{m_e}\right),$$

where

$$m=\frac{m_\mu m_{\mathrm H}}{m_\mu+m_{\mathrm H}}.$$

$$\lambda=\frac1{E_4-E_2}
=\frac1{109700\left(\frac14-\frac1{16}\right)\left(\frac m{m_e}\right)}
=2.615\times10^{-7}\ \mathrm{cm},$$
$$\frac m{m_e}=185.9,$$
$$m=185.9\times9.109\times10^{-31}=1.693\times10^{-28}\ \mathrm{kg}.$$

The mass of a proton from Tables attached:

$$m_{\mathrm H}=1.673\times10^{-27}\ \mathrm{kg},$$
$$m_\mu=\frac{m m_{\mathrm H}}{m_{\mathrm H}-m}
=\frac{1.693\times10^{-28}\times1.673\times10^{-27}}{1.673\times10^{-27}-1.693\times10^{-28}}
=1.884\times10^{-28}\ \mathrm{kg}.$$

$$\mu=\frac{m(\mathrm C)\times m(\mathrm O)}{m(\mathrm{CO})}
=\frac{12\times16}{28}=6.86\ \text{a.u.}=1{,}14\times10^{-26}\ \mathrm{kg}.$$

For interatomic distance $R$:

$$R=\frac{h}{2\pi\sqrt{2\mu B}}
=\frac{6.63\times10^{-34}}{2\times3.14\sqrt{2\times1.14\times10^{-26}\times3.81\times10^{-23}}}
=1.13\times10^{-10}\ \mathrm m=1.13\ \mathring{\mathrm A}.$$
